u Gakkai Geisei 3 Nen Shuuki Kenkyuu Happyou Kouen Rombusnhuu I, 2-5-13, October 1991, ACOUSTICAL SOC. OF JAPAN, (Automatic Generation of the Hidden Markov Network by the Successive State Splitting Algorithm), pages 73-74, XP002926556</text><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>Proceedings of 1992 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing, Vol. 1, 1992, JUN-ICHI- TAKAMI ET AL., pages I-573-I-576, XP002926554</text><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1126438A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAHI CHEMICAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHOZAKAI MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHI KASEI KOGYO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHOZAKAI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHOZAKAI MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHOZAKAI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fixed word label sequence used for recognizing a word given by an unspecified speaker is stored in vocabulary label network storage means (f).  A speech of a specified speaker is inputted, and a label sequence of registered words is created from the inputted speech by registered label sequence extracting means (d) and can be registered in the vocabulary label network storage means (f).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon la présente invention, on mémorise dans une mémoire (f) de réseau pour étiquettes de vocabulaire une séquence d'étiquettes de mots fixes, utilisée pour reconnaître un mot prononcé par un locuteur indéfini. On saisit les paroles d'un locuteur spécifié et l'on crée une séquence d'étiquettes constituée de mots enregistrés à partir des paroles saisies au moyen d'une unité d'extraction (d) de séquences d'étiquettes enregistrées. Ladite séquence d'étiquettes peut être enregistrée dans la mémoire (f) du réseau d'étiquettes de vocabulaire.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>